  "body": "The question was raised by bz [here](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=591737#c147).\n\n> What should happen when a display:none <details> has a mouse event (synthetic, clearly) fired at its first <summary>?  Should the \"open\" attribute of the <details> change?\n\nHere is the test case in [jsfiddle](https://jsfiddle.net/aethanyc/0m93g3yz/).  Both Chrome 47 and Safari 9 do not change the \"open\" attribute. Need some clarification in spec.\n",
